<title>AUSTRALIA: Macquarie shares surge on Loy Yang hopes.</title>
<headline>Macquarie shares surge on Loy Yang hopes.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Macquarie Bank Ltd surged five percent to a record high of A$9.55 on Wednesday as investors speculated on the fees likely to be earned from its role in the A$4.86 billion Loy Yang A power privatisation.</p>
<p>Macquarie's role includes that of sponsor, financial adviser and underwriter of debt and equity components of the project, which is to be listed on the Australian Stock Exchange a year after its acquisition by the Horizon Energy Consortium.</p>
<p>&quot;The deal is a big one with a lot of fees. It has to be good for them,&quot; said a Sydney broker.  </p>
<p>The Horizon Energy consortium also includes NRG Energy INC and CMS Energy Corp.</p>
<p>--Walter Watson 61-2 9373 1810</p>
